{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Session handoff — investigation concluded NOT-A-BUG; the ticket needs a disposition close\n\nState at handoff: `in_progress`, zero merged commits, no attestation. The Phase 1 comment above\nrecords a completed `/rebar-debug` investigation: **two mechanisms proven, both classified\nnot-a-bug, no code change proposed.**\n\n**Why I did not close it:** a not-a-bug disposition is a judgment about intended behaviour, and\nthis session did not run the investigation. Closing someone else's analysis on its summary line —\nwithout reading the mechanisms and agreeing with the classification — would be exactly the\nrubber-stamp the classification exists to prevent. The five ACs are also unticked and, if the\nnot-a-bug finding stands, most are moot rather than met, which is a distinction that belongs in\nthe close record.\n\n**What the next session should do:** read the Phase 1 comment, decide whether you agree with both\nclassifications, and then either\n\n- close it as a disposition — `rebar transition exemplary-hexahedral-needlefish in_progress closed\n  --class=not_a_bug` — recording in a comment that the ACs are **moot rather than satisfied**, and\n  why; or\n- if you disagree with the classification, say so with evidence and re-scope the ticket.\n\nDo not leave it `in_progress` indefinitely: a proven not-a-bug that stays open reads to `ready`\nand `next-batch` as available work and will be re-investigated by someone else. This session saw\nthat exact waste — a flaky test that two independent sessions had hit and neither recorded as a\nwork item, so it kept being rediscovered.\n\nIf the classification stands, consider whether the underlying observation (duplicate tickets only\nsurfacing after an agent is mid-implementation) deserves a separate ticket for the *workflow* gap\neven though the *mechanism* is working as designed. That is a different claim from the one\ninvestigated here."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787329341929370001,"uuid":"399543ed-7b2d-4b1c-ba85-6b349f1dc859"}